{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf phase [-h] [-r REGION] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT]\n                            [--phaser {whatshap,longphase}] [--haplotag] [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -r, --region REGION   Phase only these regions (e.g. chr20 or chr20:1-1000000, comma-separated)\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        VCF of the sample's calls to phase (default: config default_input_vcf)\n  --phaser {whatshap,longphase}\n                        Phasing tool (default: longphase for Nanopore and PacBio reads when it is\n                        installed, else whatshap). LongPhase is refused for other reads.\n  --haplotag            Also write the reads tagged with their haplotype (HP) and phase block (PS)\n                        to haplotagged.bam (.cram for CRAM input).\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n1 advanced option not shown; 'wgsextract vcf phase --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf phase --input ont.bam --vcf-input clair3.vcf.gz\n  wgsextract vcf phase --input hifi.bam --vcf-input calls.vcf.gz --haplotag\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  phased.vcf.gz (+ .tbi) and phased.blocks.tsv; with --haplotag,\n  haplotagged.bam or .cram (+ index).\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, samtools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: longphase,\n  whatshap; hours on a 30x genome.\n",
